From: csARM <csarm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] blit: never draw the blit into a 0x0 viewport

On Android (NOX11, EGL wrapper only) gl4es never learns the window size:
mainfbo_width/height stay 0, so glBlitFramebuffer() drew the quad with a
0x0 viewport and moved no pixels.  ToGL presents every frame through this
blit, so a fully loaded map stayed black.  Fall back to the destination rect.
---
 src/gl/framebuffers.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/src/gl/framebuffers.c
+++ b/src/gl/framebuffers.c
@@ -1498,6 +1498,17 @@
         fbowidth  = glstate->fbo.fbo_draw->width;
         fboheight = glstate->fbo.fbo_draw->height;
     }
+    // csARM: on Android there is no eglSurface/refreshMainFBO (NOX11 build),
+    // so mainfbo_width/height stay 0 and the blit below drew into a 0x0
+    // viewport - a silent no-op.  ToGL presents every frame exactly this way
+    // (render to an offscreen RT, glBlitFramebuffer to the window), so the
+    // engine ran a fully loaded map with a black screen.  Fall back to the
+    // blit destination rectangle.
+    if (fbowidth == 0 || fboheight == 0)
+    {
+        fbowidth  = abs( dstX1 - dstX0 );
+        fboheight = abs( dstY1 - dstY0 );
+    }
     GLint vp[4];
     memcpy(vp, &glstate->raster.viewport, sizeof(vp));
     gl4es_glViewport(0, 0, fbowidth, fboheight);
